. Maintenance restores physical support only after paid work and actual replacement materials; it does not restore food freshness. Persist treatment identity, environmental exposure, elapsed time and cumulative decay increments so a same-start treated/control pair can be compared after at least 5 elapsed simulation rounds. Compare normalized decay changes, disclose unequal exposure and uncertainty, and report no demonstrated benefit when results do not support it. An informative failure is a legitimate result, not successful preservation.\\\\nInterruption pauses paid assembly progress and releases unworked reservations safely; resume requires the same identifiable surviving project and revalidation of reach, materials and site. Cancel returns only surviving unused reserved materials once; incorporated materials remain in the partial rack, recoverable only as those actual pieces. Spent time and energy are never refunded. Pausing or canceling does not pause food decay or environmental processes. Death ends personal work, leaves the actual partial rack and food in their physical locations under ordinary death/ownership rules, and grants no refund, inheritance of mastery or continued worker activity. Completed storage can continue physically without a living operator until conditions or integrity invalidate it. No other participant acts, agrees or contributes automatically. Established checks, decay updates and lifecycle rules must execute in code, not repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No experience benefit arises from requesting, registering, studying, naming or merely inspecting without obtaining information. A completed paired comparison may qualify as verified information gain, including a documented failure, only if the actor actually observes the result and it adds personally applicable evidence. Propose at most one brief pleasure increment capped at 0.1 per distinct supported finding, with a 10-round cooldown and deduplication by functional finding and conditions; repeated identical comparisons yield none. Familiar successful food-care work may sustain modest satisfaction only through completed, useful maintenance or preservation events: cap this activity's contribution at 0.2, decay it by 0.002 per round without qualifying activity, and refresh at most once per 10 rounds. These are proposed ordinary experience contributions, implemented only through the experiment's permitted experience mechanism; never edit protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions. Do not infer pleasure merely from lower decay. No physical comfort is granted; any separately established comfort remains capped at 10. Eating still uses actual food nutrition and ordinary hunger rules, unaffected by mood.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Create reusable visual metadata for partial and complete ventilated racks: component, material palette, footprint, support height, capacity, occupied slots, work fraction, integrity, exposure/wetness, and operational state. Emit observable events for inspection findings, assembly progress, completion, loading, wetting, collapse, maintenance, unloading and measured comparison results, referencing exact affected IDs and quantities. Partial assembly must look incomplete; an intact rack may be visible without showing a preservation-success badge. Show active favorable storage conditions only when coded checks pass. Show demonstrated slower spoilage only after a valid comparison supports that result, and distinguish it from the model's current conditional rate. Failed or interrupted work must not display completion, preserved food, newly learned mastery or benefits. Only reveal environmental findings the actor can actually observe; no hidden-resource or remote-state overlays.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}}

